Building ex800 for macOS
========================

The command-line build is the same on Intel and Apple Silicon Macs. Install
the SDL2 and libpng development packages, then configure and build out of tree:

    brew install sdl2 libpng
    mkdir build-ex800
    cd build-ex800
    ../ex800-1.0.0/configure --with-video=sdl2 --with-sound=sdl2 \
        --disable-download --without-readline
    make

The executable is `src/ex800` inside the build directory.

The repository-level `build/tools/build-release.sh` script additionally builds
the Studio helper, creates an `ex800.app` bundle, copies non-system dynamic
libraries with dylibbundler and applies an ad-hoc signature. Run it natively on
the requested architecture:

    brew install sdl2 libpng dylibbundler
    build/tools/build-release.sh macos-arm64

Use `macos-x86_64` on an Intel Mac. Release distribution may require replacing
the ad-hoc signature with a Developer ID signature and notarizing the bundle.
